# PasturesScreen updated with Cow-like delete-undo flow

I applied the same delete pattern used in CowsScreen to PasturesScreen, and verified there are no other delete methods left in that screen.

## What changed
- Added snackbar + coroutine scope to PasturesScreen.
- Wired a Delete action per item with UNDO support.
- Extended PastureCard to accept `onDelete` and render a Delete button.
- Searched the project to ensure no other PasturesScreen delete paths remain.

## Key snippets

1) PasturesScreen: delete with UNDO and snackbar host
```kotlin
val snackbarHostState = remember { SnackbarHostState() }
val scope = rememberCoroutineScope()

Box(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
    Column(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
        TopAppBar(
            title = { Text("Pastures") },
            actions = {
                IconButton(onClick = onAddPastureClick) {
                    Icon(Icons.Default.Add, contentDescription = "Add Pasture")
                }
            }
        )

        // ...
        LazyColumn(
            modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp),
            verticalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp)
        ) {
            items(items = uiState.pastures, key = { it.pasture.id }) { pastureItem ->
                PastureCard(
                    pasture = pastureItem.pasture,
                    cowCount = pastureItem.cowCount,
                    onClick = { onPastureClick(pastureItem.pasture.id) },
                    onDelete = {
                        scope.launch {
                            viewModel.deletePasture(pastureItem.pasture)
                            val res = snackbarHostState.showSnackbar(
                                message = "Pasture deleted",
                                actionLabel = "UNDO",
                                duration = SnackbarDuration.Long
                            )
                            if (res == SnackbarResult.ActionPerformed) {
                                viewModel.undoDeletePasture()
                            }
                        }
                    }
                )
            }
        }
    }

    SnackbarHost(
        hostState = snackbarHostState,
        modifier = Modifier
            .align(Alignment.BottomCenter)
            .padding(16.dp)
    )
}
```

2) PastureCard: add Delete button
```kotlin
@Composable
fun PastureCard(
    pasture: Pasture,
    cowCount: Int,
    onClick: () -> Unit,
    onDelete: (() -> Unit)? = null
) {
    Card(
        = modifier Modifier
            .fillMaxWidth()
            .clickable(onClick = onClick)
    ) {
        Column(modifier = Modifier.padding(16.dp)) {
            // ... title, cows count, acres, description

            onDelete?.let {
                Spacer(modifier = Modifier.height(8.dp))
                Row(modifier = Modifier.fillMaxWidth(), horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.End) {
                    TextButton(
                        onClick = it,
                        colors = ButtonDefaults.textButtonColors(contentColor = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.error)
                    ) {
                        Text("Delete")
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## CowListScreen quick review
- Filtering and title logic look fine for now.
- LaunchedEffect uses the suspend repository call appropriately.
- Consider moving repository/ViewModel creation out of Composables (using DI or top-level ViewModel) later, but not required for this change.

Do you want me to add a guard to prevent deleting a pasture that still has cows assigned, or a confirmation dialog before delete?

