## Added “Watch Cow” toggle to Cow cards

I’ve added a watch/unwatch control on each cow card in the list and wired it to persist via the ViewModel/repository.

### Changes made

1) CowCard: added optional onToggleWatch handler with a star icon
- Filled star tinted when watched; dimmed when not.
- Placed alongside the status badge at the top-right.

```kotlin
@Composable
fun CowCard(
    cow: Cow,
    onClick: () -> Unit,
    modifier: Modifier = Modifier,
    onToggleWatch: (() -> Unit)? = null,
    onDelete: (() -> Unit)? = null
) {
    // ...
    Row(
        verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically,
        horizontalArrangement = Arrangement.spacedBy(8.dp)
    ) {
        onToggleWatch?.let {
            IconButton(onClick = it) {
                val tint = if (cow.isWatched) MaterialTheme.colorScheme.tertiary
                           else MaterialTheme.colorScheme.onSurfaceVariant.copy(alpha = 0.4f)
                Icon(
                    imageVector = androidx.compose.material.icons.Icons.Filled.Star,
                    contentDescription = if (cow.isWatched) "Unwatch" else "Watch",
                    tint = tint
                )
            }
        }
        StatusBadge(status = cow.status)
    }
    // ...
}
```

2) CowsViewModel: added toggleWatch
```kotlin
fun toggleWatch(cow: Cow) {
    viewModelScope.launch {
        repository.updateCowWatchStatus(cow.id, !cow.isWatched)
    }
}
```

3) CowsScreen: hooked up onToggleWatch
```kotlin
CowCard(
    cow = cow,
    onClick = { onCowClick(cow.id) },
    onToggleWatch = { viewModel.toggleWatch(cow) },
    onDelete = { /* existing delete with undo */ }
)
```

This uses your existing DAO method `updateCowWatchStatus(cowId, isWatched)` and UI state flow will refresh from the repository.

Want me to add a filter chip to show only “Watched” cows as well?

